\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"regression","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA (rebar-debug Phase 1, runtime-confirmed)\n\nRoot cause — a specific changeable artifact: the PRE-LOCK early-out in `sync.reconverge` (src/rebar/_store/sync.py) called `_lock.check_no_rebase_in_progress(tracker)` BEFORE acquiring the store write lock. `check_no_rebase_in_progress` (src/rebar/_store/lock.py:175) raises `RebaseGuard` on any `MERGE_HEAD`. When a peer holds the write lock and Git has created a transient `MERGE_HEAD` during the lock-owned non-fast-forward push-recovery merge, the pre-lock check saw that marker, logged 'tickets sync skipped — tracker in rebase/merge recovery state (run: rebar fsck-recover)', and returned WITHOUT ever waiting for the lock — misclassifying the lock holder's own in-progress merge as an abandoned recovery state and skipping the reconvergence round.\n\nRuntime confirmation: the reporter's deterministic two-process harness (h1_stage3.py, SHA-256 e65c356b…) reproduced hypothesis_1=TRUE on origin/main (dddaa60): while MERGE_HEAD existed and the write lock was held by the push process (pid matched), the peer reconverge emitted the WARNING from funcName 'reconverge' at sync.py:300 and returned in 0.0001s (waited_for_write_lock=false); after the merge released, the push succeeded, MERGE_HEAD cleared, lock cleared, local==remote.\n\nAttribution (caused_by): cindery-lithe-acaciarat (e699-7df5-bd51-40f6) moved the push-retry recovery merge UNDER the write lock and added the in-lock `check_no_rebase_in_progress` re-check, but its plan explicitly preserved the pre-existing pre-lock check as an early exit. Before that change the push-retry merge ran unlocked, so no lock-owned MERGE_HEAD existed for the pre-lock check to misclassify; the change introduced the interaction that made the previously-correct pre-lock classification wrong. Close class: regression.\n\nFix: remove the pre-lock recovery-state early-out so classification is authoritative only after the write lock is acquired. Fetch stays outside the lock; the in-lock `check_no_rebase_in_progress` guard in `_do_reconverge` still refuses a genuinely stranded marker (one that survives lock acquisition) and directs the operator to rebar fsck-recover. RED→GREEN: tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py::test_reconverge_waits_for_a_lock_owned_push_recovery_merge (barrier-based, RED on the pre-lock warning before the fix, GREEN after) and tests/unit/test_store_sync_reconverge.py::test_reconverge_refuses_a_stranded_merge_marker_after_lock_acquisition (preserves stranded refusal via the in-lock guard). Harness now reports hypothesis_1=FALSE.","timestamp":1787938503625808001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operational evidence for AC6 (Focused tests, lint, type checking, and full suite pass) [non-codebase]:\n\nLanded via Gerrit change 2324 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2324), patchset 2, commit 4de4d30cf904, now MERGED to main.\n\n- Verified +1 (CI gate): GitHub Actions run 33198160020 => success (full build/test/lint/typecheck on the patchset-2 tree, both macOS and Linux). This is the authoritative full-suite + lint + typecheck attestation.\n- LLM-Review +1 (code-review gate): PASS.\n- Gerrit submit requirements met: LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1 AND 0 unresolved comments; submittable=True; then submitted => status MERGED.\n\nLocal focused runs (worktree venv, /Users/joeoakhart/debug/consensual-drake):\n- New RED->GREEN regression test tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py::test_reconverge_waits_for_a_lock_owned_push_recovery_merge: RED on unfixed code (pre-lock reconverge fsck-recover warning), GREEN after removing the pre-lock early-out.\n- Preservation test tests/unit/test_store_sync_reconverge.py::test_reconverge_refuses_a_stranded_merge_marker_after_lock_acquisition: GREEN (AC3, in-lock guard still refuses + directs to rebar fsck-recover).\n- Affected suites: 42 passed; ruff check + format-check clean; mypy typecheck clean.\n- Reporter harness h1_stage3.py: hypothesis_1 flipped true -> false after the fix.","timestamp":1787942405847032001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787628550521586001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"97af21d3-11d2-49ef-9f4b-5d2ed4551269","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"5cda-6f1e-533f-4e0b"},{"link_uuid":"afcc52b7-5353-48c1-aaef-37f091fa40a1","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"e699-7df5-bd51-40f6"},{"link_uuid":"f7202798-7c00-4889-aef8-59752ffd2460","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1b21-1d1c-182f-4686"},{"link_uuid":"ed85f182-7a54-45a5-88be-b34a737a17d5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b831-4aa7-0a4a-4139"}],"description":"## Context\n\nA deterministic two-process harness confirms that `sync.reconverge` inspects tracker recovery markers before acquiring the store write lock. Process A performs the non-fast-forward push recovery merge introduced under `cindery-lithe-acaciarat`. It owns the write lock while Git creates `MERGE_HEAD`. Process B calls `sync.reconverge`, sees that marker at the pre-lock early exit, emits an `fsck-recover` warning, and returns without waiting for the lock.\n\nProcess A then completes successfully. Its merge marker and lock clear, and the local and remote tips match. The warning therefore diagnoses an abandoned recovery state when the marker belongs to the process that owns the lock. The skipped reconvergence round also delays freshness. The enrichment drain is not involved.\n\nThe harness is `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar-debug-harness-20260824/h1_stage3.py`. Its SHA-256 is `e65c356bdc288c8729d5170524b89daca01e667600c2b385e4211c50e6083764`.\n\n`cindery-lithe-acaciarat` correctly moved the push recovery merge under the write lock and added an in-lock recovery check. Its plan review explicitly preserved the existing pre-lock check as an early exit. That check predates the lock-owned push recovery interaction and cannot distinguish a stranded merge from work performed by the lock holder.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Make recovery-state classification in `sync.reconverge` authoritative only after the store write lock is acquired.\n- Preserve fetch outside the store write lock.\n- Preserve the in-lock `check_no_rebase_in_progress` guard in `_do_reconverge`.\n- Add a deterministic concurrency test with state-based barriers. Pause a push recovery merge after `MERGE_HEAD` appears, start a peer reconverge, confirm that it remains pending, then release the merge.\n- Preserve refusal and recovery guidance when a merge marker remains after lock acquisition.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A peer reconverge does not return or emit an `fsck-recover` warning solely because a lock-owning push recovery merge has created `MERGE_HEAD`.\n- [x] After the push recovery merge releases the lock, both operations exit successfully, `MERGE_HEAD` is absent, the lock is clear, local and remote tips match, and all seeded events remain reachable.\n- [x] A stranded merge marker found after lock acquisition still blocks reset or merge mutation and directs the operator to `rebar fsck-recover`.\n- [x] Fetch remains outside the store write lock, and existing fetch coordination and best-effort lock timeout behavior remain unchanged.\n- [x] The regression test uses synchronization barriers instead of a wall-clock race.\n- [x] [non-codebase] Focused tests, lint, type checking, and the full suite pass.\n  provenance: environment=GitHub Actions CI (run 33198160020) + worktree venv (/Users/joeoakhart/debug/consensual-drake/.venv); principal=RebarBotNava <joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com>; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — Gerrit change 2324 patchset 2 earned Verified +1 from CI run 33198160020 (success), which executed the full build/test/lint/typecheck suite on macOS and Linux; local focused suites (42 passed), ruff check+format-check, and mypy all ran green in the worktree venv.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/sync.py","reason":"Move authoritative recovery-state classification under the store write lock without moving fetch."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py","reason":"Prove a peer reconverge waits for a lock-owned push recovery merge and preserves events."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_store_sync_reconverge.py","reason":"Preserve stranded-merge refusal and fetch timeout behavior."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","1b21-1d1c-182f-4686"],["relates_to","b831-4aa7-0a4a-4139"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6a745300-9605-4afb-8d82-223ef7ccf861","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["concurrency","tracker","recovery"],"ticket_id":"042d-7bfc-3409-410a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"sync.reconverge misclassifies a lock-owned push recovery merge as abandoned","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["fc657692-f957-4fef-afa6-377b2d44a74c","46d95154-f974-44e2-bfad-600f408f0b60","8bf15adb-225b-40ad-98e1-621297f46768","af9ec88e-49bd-4e92-b9ea-8be0d64878cb","f7202798-7c00-4889-aef8-59752ffd2460","ed85f182-7a54-45a5-88be-b34a737a17d5","be821e2d-f619-4db1-81bc-2dc4cbd9edd9","38d25e59-76b8-4f7e-bddd-3d6618cd5ff6","d4c503de-47b6-4659-82bc-61b3dd69926e","7ac88e6f-0245-4d96-b9c6-1b5f02fd5d8f","6a745300-9605-4afb-8d82-223ef7ccf861","77a84e5c-5852-4dc4-9f91-012f121e46fc"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787949897920935001,"uuid":"87441cbe-6cfb-42ed-adaf-180e0d9b2285"}